<title>THAILAND: Thai central bank schedule for Nov notes auction.</title>
<headline>Thai central bank schedule for Nov notes auction.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand said on Monday it had scheduled weekly auctions for a total of 13 billion baht ($520 million) in short-term central bank notes in November and for bonds of its Financial Institutions Development Fund. Here is the auction schedule:</p>
<p>Bank of Thailand's notes</p>
<p>    Date	  Tenor (Days)	Amount</p>
<p>					(million baht)</p>
<p>   1/11/96	  28		  2,000</p>
<p>   1/11/96	  98		  1,000</p>
<p>   1/11/96	 183		  1,000</p>
<p>   8/11/96	  28		  2,000</p>
<p>  15/11/96	  28		  2,000</p>
<p>  15/11/96	  98		  1,000</p>
<p>  22/11/96	  28		  2,000</p>
<p>  29/11/96	  28		  2,000</p>
<p>Financial Institutions Development Fund Bonds</p>
<p>    Date	  Tenor (Years)	 Amount</p>
<p>				     (million baht)</p>
<p>   8/11/96	 2		    3,000</p>
<p>  22/11/96	 3		    2,000</p>
<p>(US$1 = 25 baht)</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642</p>
</text>
